url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingqin2/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingqin2/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingqin2/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingqin2/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingqin2/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingqin2/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingqin2/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bingqin2/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-13T05:07:26Z","updated_at":"2026-09-13T05:07:26Z","body":"Thanks for checking it on the RC. From the description of #72205, limiting `POST /auth/token` to the configured client is deliberate: the endpoint is unauthenticated, so before the change the credentials of any confidential client in a shared realm were valid Airflow logins. A separate `airflow-bootstrap` client is therefore not meant to work any more, and giving the `airflow` client's service account the roles you list is the supported way to do what the bootstrap client did.\n\nThe trade-off to be aware of: the `airflow` client secret, which the API server already holds for the login flow, now also mints an admin API token, so it deserves the same handling the bootstrap secret had.\n\n@potiuk wrote #72205 and can say whether a dedicated bootstrap client is intended to come back in some form (for example an allow-list of client ids). If not, this issue can be closed once keycloak 0.10.0 is published.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/comments/5651300590/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bingqin2","id":126308766,"node_id":"U_kgDOB4dRng","ava